							"a": "In the Agentic Web era, external agents carry passports adhering to the **RFC-010 W3C DID Open Passport** standard when interacting across organizations. However, claims asserted by external passports do not imply unconditional acceptance by local systems.\n\nDROS enforces **'Open Identity Flow, Localized Deterministic Hard Interception'**: the local **GuardVM gateway** uses $O(1)$ Capability Bitmaps to deterministically isolate permissions. Even if an external agent presents high-privilege claims, the local GuardVM enforces C-ABI interception within $26.1\\ \\mu\\text{s}$, blocking unauthorized access attempts locally."
