						"a": "Traditional LLM Agent or RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) solutions rely heavily on vector databases (Vector DB) and probabilistic models. They attempt to reduce error rates by 'optimizing prompts' or 'increasing retrieval accuracy', but this is merely playing with 'probabilities' and cannot provide safety guarantees beyond the documented boundary.\n\nDROS employs a disruptive architecture of **pure physical file topology + O(1) microkernel engine + runtime strict discipline**. We do not waste time 'optimizing probability', but rather **'constrain probability with a deterministic physical structure'**. All contracts and permissions are unrolled into binary Bitmap arrays at Compile-time, and during Runtime, every single Agent operation is subjected to physical-layer verification with a latency of less than 1 millisecond."
