							"a": "Traditional IP tracing only identifies the 'host device (machine-level)' that sent the request. It is easily obscured by proxies or VPNs, and suffers from severe Context Loss—making it impossible to distinguish which specific Agent role or session inside the host executed the action. Consequently, enterprises cannot clarify specific attribution during compliance audits.\n\nDROS's attribution mechanism operates **by execution (per execution behavior)**, precisely positioned at the FFI boundary between Tool Invocation and OS system calls. Agents must carry capability credentials cryptographically signed by DROS CA. The system cryptographically binds the Agent Identity (UUID), parameters, and context to generate an unforgeable 'execution fingerprint.' This allows tracing directly to the **Agent-level**, providing enterprises with clear liability mitigation boundaries and active defense while securing the system."
